.TH SDL_DEFINE_COLORSPACE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_DEFINE_COLORSPACE \- A macro for defining custom
.BR SDL_Colorspace
formats.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_pixels.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_DEFINE_COLORSPACE(type, range, primaries, transfer, matrix, chroma) \(rs
.BI "    (((Uint32)(type) << 28) | ((Uint32)(range) << 24) | ((Uint32)(chroma) << 20) | \(rs
.BI "    ((Uint32)(primaries) << 10) | ((Uint32)(transfer) << 5) | ((Uint32)(matrix) << 0))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
For example, defining
.BR SDL_COLORSPACE_SRGB
looks like this:

.IP
.EX
SDL_DEFINE_COLORSPACE(SDL_COLOR_TYPE_RGB,
                      SDL_COLOR_RANGE_FULL,
                      SDL_COLOR_PRIMARIES_BT709,
                      SDL_TRANSFER_CHARACTERISTICS_SRGB,
                      SDL_MATRIX_COEFFICIENTS_IDENTITY,
                      SDL_CHROMA_LOCATION_NONE)
.EE
.PP

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I type
the type of the new format, probably an
.BR SDL_ColorType
value\[char46]
.TP
.I range
the range of the new format, probably a
.BR SDL_ColorRange
value\[char46]
.TP
.I primaries
the primaries of the new format, probably an
.BR SDL_ColorPrimaries
value\[char46]
.TP
.I transfer
the transfer characteristics of the new format, probably an
.BR SDL_TransferCharacteristics
value\[char46]
.TP
.I matrix
the matrix coefficients of the new format, probably an
.BR SDL_MatrixCoefficients
value\[char46]
.TP
.I chroma
the chroma sample location of the new format, probably an
.BR SDL_ChromaLocation
value\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a format value in the style of
.BR SDL_Colorspace \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

